Tests only. No implementation, no fix. 40 of 48 assertions observed failing;
red captured verbatim at docs/delivery/evidence/v6-20260903T195241Z/wave4-telemetry/
02-tests-failing.log.

scripts/validate/telemetry_contract_audit.mjs (19 checks, 15 red)
  Source/build contract: the sendBeacon module, the telemetryCollect and
  telemetryPrune Cloud Functions, the same-origin /api/telemetry Hosting rewrite
  (D-04: built on the already-working Functions path), a 30-day retention that
  the published sentence prints verbatim, and TEL-SRC-13 — the source-level rule
  that excludes the 2026-07-09 outage mode: no getSnapshot()/getServerSnapshot()
  returning a freshly constructed value, no device API in a useState initializer.

  TEL-183 is a BIDIRECTIONAL lock. Either no instrumentation exists and the
  legacy "no analytics, no trackers, no cookies" claim stands, or the
  instrumentation exists and both published lines carry the reconciled strings.
  Half the work fails it in either order. That is R-183 made mechanical.

tests/telemetry/collector.contract.mjs (21 checks, 21 red)
  The collector's pure logic off Firebase: the nine R-87 event names, envelope
  rejection codes that never echo the payload back, sanitisation down to exactly
  {at, name, section, value} with the timestamp coarsened to the minute, the
  retention boundary, hand-computed dwell medians and drop-off rates, and the
  R-175 path — an unobserved window yields a not-observable record with a
  reason, never a zero, and R-88 never reopens a section on a value nobody
  measured.

tests/overhaul/telemetry-first-party.spec.ts (8 checks, 4 red)
  Browser-observable. TEL-FP-01 holds the site's zero-third-party-request
  property open across instrumentation (22 requests, one origin, measured in
  03-network-trace-baseline.json), and refuses to pass vacuously.

